                <h2 class="post-title">On Malfunctioning Heaters and Unsolicited Naps</h2>
                <div class="post-content">
                    <p>The heating in my car is broken. Or maybe it's just temperamental. It has a personality, this car. Mostly a bad one. Tonight, it decided to fill the cabin with cold, damp air, which felt fitting for the occasion.</p>

                    <p>There's a specific kind of silence that follows an argument. It's not peaceful. It's heavy. It's filled with all the things you didn't say, and all the things you did. You can almost hear the words hanging in the air, refusing to dissipate. The radio was playing something by The National, I think. Something about sorrow. I almost turned it off, but the silence felt worse.</p>

                    <blockquote>"I don't want to be alone tonight."</blockquote>

                    <p>Funny how a few simple words can dismantle every defense you've ever built. Funny how they can make you say "Fine" when every rational part of your brain is screaming "No".</p>

                    <p>And then, she fell asleep. Just like that. One moment, we were encased in that thick, angry silence. The next, she was just... gone. Head against the window, breathing softly. The argument, the tension, none of it seemed to matter anymore. It was absurd. It was infuriating. And it was, in a strange way, a relief.</p>

                    <p>Her head eventually ended up on my shoulder. I didn't move. I just kept driving, hyper-aware of the slight weight, the warmth seeping through two layers of fabric. It's a weight I haven't felt in years, but my body remembers it. My body remembers everything.</p>

                    <p>She's lighter now. I noticed. It's one of those details you register without meaning to. A quiet, unwelcome piece of data filed away in the back of your mind.</p>

                    <div class="audio-player">
                        <span class="audio-title">Now Playing: The National - "Sorrow"</span>
                        <div class="progress-bar-container">
                            <div class="progress-bar"></div>
