        <p>The most terrifying part? The part no one writes songs about? It's not the arguments, not the screaming matches. It's the quiet moments after. The moment she curls up in your arms and you realize her entire, chaotic universe now rests in the fragile space between your heartbeats. And you know, with absolute certainty, that if you move, if you breathe wrong, it will all shatter. And you will <span class="highlight">shatter</span> with it.</p>

